  "summary": "Telegram-controlled remote shell on the host running the bot",
  "details": "infogram-bot registers a Telegram MessageHandler whose handler passes message text from remote Telegram users into subprocess.check_output(..., shell=True) on the machine running the bot. Users in the OWNERS list can run arbitrary shell commands, execute Python/other binaries, read and exfiltrate files (via 'take' and 'get all' commands), delete files, and dump environment variables from the host. In group chats, the '.sh ' prefix branch extends shell execution to any group member, broadening the set of remote parties who can drive host commands. pyproject.toml ships with placeholder author metadata ('Aapka Naam', 'you@example.com') and a homepage/repository URL containing 'YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME', so the publisher of the package that receives the Telegram bot token and controls the OWNERS list is not identifiable.",
